    <!-- Brightness-nits mapping. Each value is the backlight float MediaTek's composer gets:
         it writes level 1 + 20478 * value to lcd-backlight (range from max_brightness, 20479),
         and the panel takes that level as is (0x51, 0-4095). So value (L - 1) / 20478 is panel
         level L. The nits are stock's calibration (/odm/etc/dsi_o16u_*_mi.xml: TargetNit and
         PanelBrCl, MiBlLut below level 101 where its PCC factor is 1), the median of the four
         panel variants. Stock reaches these levels through Xiaomi's display service, which the
         ROM doesn't ship. Level 15 is the minimum (stock goes to ~10, but the 44-0f-0c panel
         needs ~28 for the same 2 nits); 4094 the maximum, 4095 being the panel's peak mode. -->
    <screenBrightnessMap>
        <point><value>0.000683661</value><nits>3.27</nits></point> <!-- level 15 -->
